# =============================================================================
# Sunrooof BOM Builder — environment configuration EXAMPLE
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# IMPORTANT: The RUNTIME app reads NO environment variables. It is a static,
# client-only Next.js site — there is no server, DB, or API. Nothing below is
# needed to run `npm run dev` / `npm run build` / `npm run start`.
#
# These variables only matter for the DEPLOY tooling (Vercel CLI) and for
# (optional) local regeneration of data from Excel masters. Copy this file to
# `.env` (or export the vars in your shell) and fill in real values. NEVER commit
# real secrets. Placeholders below explain what each value should contain.
# =============================================================================

# --- Vercel deployment (secret) ----------------------------------------------
# A Vercel access token with deploy rights to the Magppie Silverstone team.
# Create one at: https://vercel.com/account/tokens  (keep it out of git).
# Used as:  vercel deploy --prod --yes --scope $VERCEL_SCOPE --token $VERCEL_TOKEN
VERCEL_TOKEN=your_vercel_access_token_here

# The Vercel team/scope slug this project deploys under.
VERCEL_SCOPE=magppiesilverstonepvtltd

# Vercel project + org identifiers (non-secret; already in source/.vercel/project.json
# on the maintainer's machine — reproduced here for reference).
VERCEL_PROJECT_ID=prj_pMMCW9kHnmMwWYCua3pQkktsz2ew
VERCEL_ORG_ID=team_3kNUUimkx3oLM7Mfudka1f6S
VERCEL_PROJECT_NAME=sunrooof-bomb-builder

# --- Data regeneration (local, optional) -------------------------------------
# Absolute paths to the Excel master workbooks used by the build-*.js scripts.
# Currently these paths are HARDCODED near the top of each script (const FILE = ...).
# If you refactor the scripts to read from env, wire them to these:
MASTER_INVENTORY_XLSX=/absolute/path/to/Inventory SUNROOOF (5).xlsx
PARTS_BOM_XLSX=/absolute/path/to/parts bom (2).xlsx
# Legacy catalog sources (used only by build-data.js):
CATALOG_MAIN_XLSX=/absolute/path/to/SUNROOOF BOM MAIN.xlsx
CATALOG_DETAIL_XLSX=/absolute/path/to/SUNROOOF BOM DETAIL.xlsx

# --- NOT USED (documented so you don't go looking) ---------------------------
# There are NO database URLs, NO third-party API keys, NO OAuth client secrets,
# NO JWT/session secrets, and NO analytics keys in this project. If you add a
# backend later, define its secrets here and document them in docs/11.

